.TH KENTSCRIPT 1 "August 2026" "KentScript v3.1.0" "User Manual"
.SH NAME
kentscript \- KentScript systems programming language
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kentscript
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR ...]
.br
.B kentscript
[\fB\-c\fR \fICODE\fR]
.br
.B kentscript
.RI (no arguments)
.SH DESCRIPTION
KentScript is a systems programming language combining Python-like syntax with
C-level low-level features: pointers, syscalls, unsafe memory, inline assembly,
and bare-metal kernel development. The \fBkentscript\fR binary is the single
entry point for running, building, debugging, and inspecting KentScript programs.
.PP
With no arguments, \fBkentscript\fR starts an interactive REPL with
Tab-autocomplete and command history.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBrun\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
Compile and run a KentScript file in interpreter mode.
.TP
\fBbuild\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-O\fR\fILVL\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIOUT\fR]
Compile to a native binary via the C transpiler.
.TP
\fBdebug\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-break\fR \fILINE\fR] [\fB\-\-stop\fR] [\fB\-\-steps\fR \fIN\fR]
Launch the interactive step-through debugger. KentScript programs run inside a
real debugger that pauses at breakpoints and after each statement, printing the
current source line and live state. Set one or more breakpoints with repeated
\fB\-\-break\fR \fILINE\fR flags (1-based line numbers), \fB\-\-stop\fR to pause
before the first statement, or \fB\-\-steps\fR \fIN\fR to auto-stop after \fIN\fR
steps. At the \fB(debug)\fR prompt use:
.RS
.TP
\fBs\fR, \fBstep\fR
Step into the next statement (enters function calls).
.TP
\fBn\fR, \fBnext\fR
Step over the next statement (does not enter calls).
.TP
\fBc\fR, \fBcontinue\fR
Resume execution until the next breakpoint or program end.
.TP
\fBb\fR \fILINE\fR, \fBbreak\fR \fILINE\fR
Set a breakpoint at \fILINE\fR.
.TP
\fBp\fR \fIVAR\fR, \fBprint\fR \fIVAR\fR
Print the current value of variable \fIVAR\fR.
.TP
\fBl\fR, \fBlocals\fR
List all variables in the current scope.
.TP
\fBbt\fR
Show the current call stack (backtrace).
.TP
\fBq\fR, \fBquit\fR
End the debug session.
.TP
\fBh\fR, \fBhelp\fR
Show the debugger command list.
.RE
.TP
\fBinfo\fR
Show system information (platform, CPU, memory, Python version).
.TP
\fBaudit\fR \fIFILE\fR
Forensic binary audit: 10-part test ladder plus freestanding tools.
.TP
\fBprivilege_report\fR
9-level truth ladder: userland to bare metal privilege analysis.
.TP
\fBring0\fR \fIFILE\fR [\fB\-\-arch\fR \fIARCH\fR]
Compile to a Ring 0 kernel image.
.TP
\fBkernel\-dev\fR \fIFILE\fR
Generate kernel development files: GDT, IDT, scheduler, vmem, syscall C files.
.TP
\fBminios\fR \fIFILE\fR
MiniOS bare-metal OS builder (AArch64 QEMU-virt target).
.TP
\fBhardware\fR
Hardware discovery, MMIO read, MSR access.
.TP
\fBwasm\fR \fIFILE\fR
Compile KentScript to WebAssembly (.wasm) and execute.
.TP
\fBsecurity\fR
Start the KSecurity ethical cybersecurity and penetration testing console
(interactive: Tab-autocomplete modules/options, history recall).
.TP
\fBide\fR [\fB\-\-port\fR \fIPORT\fR] [\fB\-\-root\fR \fIDIR\fR]
Launch the built-in web IDE on localhost (default port 8000).
Professional code editor with KentScript syntax highlighting, interactive
shell/REPL panel, LSP (completion, hover, diagnostics), file browser,
frosted glass UI, responsive layout, state persistence, and auto port retry.
The bottom panel has a \fBProblems\fR view (live diagnostics from the LSP and
the server-side analyzer) and a \fBDebug Console\fR. Click the editor gutter to
toggle a breakpoint, then use Run & Debug to start a session; the Debug Console
shows the \fB(debug)\fR prompt where the same \fBs\fR/\fBn\fR/\fBc\fR/\fBp\fR/\fBq\fR
commands drive the running program, with the current line highlighted inline.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c\fR \fICODE\fR
Execute KentScript code directly from the command line (like \fBpython \-c\fR).
.TP
\fB\-O\fR\fI0\fR, \fB\-O\fR\fI1\fR, \fB\-O\fR\fI2\fR, \fB\-O\fR\fI3\fR
Optimization level for the C transpiler (default: \-O2).
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIFILE\fR
Specify output file name for \fBbuild\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable debug symbols and debug output.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version information.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.
.SH LANGUAGE FEATURES
.SS Variables
.Ex
let x: i64 = 42;
let mut y = 0;
const PI = 3.14159;
.Ee
.SS Types
.Ex
i8, i16, i32, i64, i128
u8, u16, u32, u64, u128
f16, f32, f64, f128
isize, usize
int, uint, float, bool, str, string, char, ptr, void, any
.Ee
.SS Functions
.Ex
func add(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 {
    return a + b;
}

async func fetch(url: str) -> str { ... }
.Ee
.SS Classes and Structs
.Ex
class Point {
    init(self, x: i64, y: i64) {
        self.x = x;
        self.y = y;
    }
}

struct Vec3 { x: f64; y: f64; z: f64; }
.Ee
.SS Enums and Traits
.Ex
enum Color { Red, Green, Blue; }

trait Drawable {
    draw();
}

impl Circle for Drawable {
    func draw(self) { ... }
}
.Ee
.SS Control Flow
.Ex
if x > 0 { ... } elif x < 0 { ... } else { ... }
for i in range(10) { ... }
while running { ... }
match x {
    case 1: { ... }
    case 2: { ... }
    default: { ... }
}
.Ee
.SS Unsafe Blocks
.Ex
unsafe {
    let p = malloc(1024);
    ptr_write(p, 0, 42);
    let v = ptr_read(p);
    free(p);
}
.Ee
.SS Borrow Checker
.Ex
let data = [1, 2, 3];
let r = borrow(data, false);
:: use r ...
release(r);
.Ee
.SS Comments
.Ex
:: single line comment
/// documentation comment
/* block comment */
.Ee
.SH STANDARD LIBRARY
The standard library lives in \fIstdlib/\fR and is imported with
\fBimport\fR. All modules auto-complete in the REPL and VSCode.
.SS Core
.TP
\fBimport os;\fR
File and OS operations (getpid, mkdir, read_file, getenv, ...).
.TP
\fBimport math;\fR
Math functions (sin, cos, sqrt, log, pow, ...).
.TP
\fBimport json;\fR
JSON encoding/decoding (dumps, loads).
.TP
\fBimport datetime;\fR
Date/time parsing and formatting.
.TP
\fBimport random;\fR
Random number generation (random, randint, choice, shuffle).
.TP
\fBimport strings;\fR
String manipulation (upper, lower, contains, split, replace, ...).
.TP
\fBimport regex;\fR
Regular expressions (match, search, findall, sub, ...).
.TP
\fBimport collections;\fR
Data structures (deque, counter, namedtuple, ordered_dict, ...).
.TP
\fBimport itertools;\fR
Iteration tools (chain, product, combinations, islice, ...).
.TP
\fBimport functools;\fR
Functional programming (partial, reduce, lru_cache, ...).
.SS I/O and Networking
.TP
\fBimport fileio;\fR
File I/O operations.
.TP
\fBimport http;\fR
HTTP client (get, post, put, delete, stream, with_cookies).
.TP
\fBimport socket;\fR
TCP/UDP socket wrapper (tcp, udp, connect, bind, listen, ...).
.TP
\fBimport network;\fR
Network utilities.
.TP
\fBimport email;\fR
SMTP/IMAP email client (send, fetch, IMAP mailbox access).
.SS Web
.TP
\fBimport web;\fR
Web framework \- routing with path params, CORS, sessions, file uploads, rate limiting.
.TP
\fBimport webui;\fR
45+ styled UI components (hero, pricing, kanban, charts, chat, etc). Dark/light/midnight themes. No external CSS.
.TP
\fBimport webserver;\fR
HTTP server with static files, directory listing, MIME detection.
.TP
\fBimport openapi;\fR
OpenAPI 3.0 spec generator with path params and schemas.
.TP
\fBimport ide;\fR
Built-in web IDE: professional code editor with syntax highlighting, interactive
shell/REPL (uses real kentscript binary), LSP completion/hover/diagnostics,
file browser, frosted glass UI, responsive layout. The bottom panel combines a
live \fBProblems\fR view (LSP + server analyzer diagnostics) with a
\fBDebug Console\fR; set breakpoints by clicking the gutter and drive a real
step-through debug session via the Run & Debug controls. Launch with
\fBkentscript ide\fR or \fBide.start()\fR.
.TP
\fBimport websocket;\fR
WebSocket client and server with callbacks and broadcast.
.TP
\fBimport graphql;\fR
GraphQL client (query, mutate over HTTP).
.SS Data
.TP
\fBimport sqlite;\fR
SQLite database (built\-in). connect, execute, query, transactions.
.TP
\fBimport postgres;\fR
PostgreSQL driver (psycopg2\-binary). Full execute/fetch/transactions.
.TP
\fBimport mysql;\fR
MySQL driver (mysql\-connector\-python). Full execute/fetch/transactions.
.TP
\fBimport mariadb;\fR
MariaDB driver (falls back to mysql\-connector). Full execute/fetch.
.TP
\fBimport sql;\fR
Query builder \- select, insert, update, delete, joins, aggregates. Works with all SQL backends.
.TP
\fBimport csv;\fR
CSV reading/writing.
.TP
\fBimport excel;\fR
XLSX read/write (no pip needed).
.TP
\fBimport dataframe;\fR
Pandas-like DataFrame (filter, sort, groupby).
.TP
\fBimport image;\fR
ImageMagick bridge (resize, crop, convert).
